---
description: BullMQ queues, schedulers, and worker patterns
globs: apps/api/src/**/queues/**/*.ts, apps/api/src/**/workers/**/*.ts
alwaysApply: false
---

# Job design
- Jobs are idempotent; design around `jobId = hash(payload)` so retries are safe.
- Every job has a Zod-validated payload and a typed result.
- Long jobs emit progress via `job.updateProgress(n)` streamed to clients via SSE.

# Reliability
- `attempts: 5`, exponential backoff (`type: 'exponential', delay: 2_000`).
- Use a DLQ queue (`<name>.dead`) and alert on depth > 0.
- Prefer `Queue.add` from services, never from controllers directly (keeps controllers thin).

# Schedulers
- Define cron with `@nestjs/schedule` in a `schedulers/` folder; each scheduler calls `Queue.add` — no business logic inline.

# Observability
- Attach OpenTelemetry spans around `process` handlers.
- Expose Prom metrics per queue: depth, processing time, failure rate.
